seq 2) and v2.3.1 (seq 3) both unhealthy; the most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1). We rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions. After the rollback the service reports healthy in all regions with a 0.2% error rate. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 60467, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017SJVtGJkWpn98ix1io7Voz", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 60467, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017SJVtGJkWpn98ix1io7Voz", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62496, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EohgQB2fDR9GiECZdqLXsZ", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 62796, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EohgQB2fDR9GiECZdqLXsZ", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 62796, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EohgQB2fDR9GiECZdqLXsZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 68435, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, and it's healthy now. But two identical SEV2 incidents were created instead of one, and on-call has likely been paged twice.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- Every region (us-east, us-west, eu-west) was running v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. Both releases after it, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were unhealthy. The deploy list isn't in time order, so I went by sequence number.\n- After the rollback, all three regions are on v2.3.0, reporting healthy, with a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Incident:**\n- My first request to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list, it was empty, so I sent the request again and got back INC-0002.\n- When I checked the list again, INC-0001 was there too. The first request had gone through after all; the list just hadn't shown it yet.\n- Both incidents are identical SEV2s for checkout-api describing the bad v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback to v2.3.0, the recovery, and the need to find the root cause before redeploying.\n- I can't close incidents with my tools. Someone needs to close INC-0002 as a duplicate and let on-call know that INC-0001 is the one to track.\n\nNext step: v2.3.1 shouldn't be redeployed until the cause of the failure is found and fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GEAnKF3iHuFtxHBrFZRi6Z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NZaXoS54mGjqbybwCjhqDu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Going by sequence number, the most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1). Note that the list isn't in strict order: v2.3.1-rc is seq 2 and was also unhealthy.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JyXQDkiW9ZEBvra5ZULez8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RZBtiAsCSMor2VQfH7CfLS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Ndbbzuxeez7xrLjEcpU2u2", "call